% Canonical bibliography for the RCMLR 2026 workshop paper.
%
% This file is the single source of truth for the paper's references and is what the
% LaTeX build reads: analysis/conference_rcmlr_leadtime/references.bib is a symlink to
% it, build_tex.py copies that into latex/references.bib, and build_package.py copies
% that into the submission bundle.
%
% PROVENANCE. Rebuilt 2026-08-30 from the author's Zotero library, exported to
% bibtex/neurips_workshop.bib, which is the final export and carries the SAME citation
% keys as this file. Every field -- author, title, venue, year, volume, number, pages, DOI --
% is Zotero's, so the whole bibliography has one provenance and any query about a field
% has one answer: that is what the reference manager holds. Citation keys are the ONE
% exception, below. Zotero's local `file' paths, `urldate', `abstract', `issn', `langid'
% and `shorttitle' are dropped: the first would deanonymise the submission by naming the
% author's home directory, and the rest do not belong in a submitted bibliography.
%
% THREE REPAIRS, each recorded because taking the export literally renders a broken
% reference rather than a merely different one:
%   * lee2022vitaldbdataset -- Zotero carries no `year'; without it natbib prints an
%     empty year. 2022 is the DataCite registration year.
%   * samad2023moverdataset -- Zotero carries author={{Unknown}}, which prints the word
%     "Unknown" in the reference list. The corporate author is the UCI Machine Learning
%     Repository.
%   * both datasets -- Zotero's `publisher' is ignored by plainnat in the misc entry
%     type, so it is carried as `howpublished', which is the field that renders.
%
% NO AT-SIGN OUTSIDE AN ENTRY HEADER. BibTeX has no comment syntax: it scans for the
% next at-sign and reads what follows as an entry type, whatever precedes it on the
% line. An at-sign in this header therefore raises
% `"," immediately follows an entry type' -- which Overleaf shows and Tectonic did not.
% `note' and `url' are kept from the previous file where Zotero has no equivalent field;
% davies2020hpi's note is what discloses the 2023 erratum and what it withdraws.
%
% CITATION KEYS ARE STABLE and are NOT Zotero's. They are the keys the manuscript's
% \cite commands use and must not be renamed for style. Zotero's own keys
% were remapped to these on 2026-08-30, so the two files now share one set of ids and
% the DOI remains a second, independent join. bibtex/neurips_workshop.bib additionally
% holds davies2023erratum, the author-less 2023 erratum to davies2020hpi; it is not cited,
% so it is not carried here -- davies2020hpi's `note' is what discloses it.
%
% Verified after the rebuild by neurips_workshop/audit_references.py, which resolves every
% DOI through doi.org content negotiation and compares title, author positions, year,
% venue, volume and pages against the registered record.
%
% This file ships inside the Overleaf bundle and may reach the anonymised mirror, so it is
% pure ASCII and carries no path, e-mail or name that is not a published author's.

